        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "aa968de9-6abe-5388-9303-fbe3d7660a88",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Joey Ramone, Jeffrey Ross Hyman, Miles Hunt, Billy Duffy, Morgan Nicholls, Pete Howard\n- Bands and Projects: Ramones, Vent 414, The Wonder Stuff, The Cult, Senseless Things, The Streets, Muse, The Clash, Eat\n- Products: Don't Worry About Me\n- Roles: musician, singer-songwriter, guitarist, lead vocalist, drummer\n\nFacts:\n- Jeffrey Ross Hyman was born on May 19, 1951, and was professionally known as Joey Ramone.\n- Joey Ramone was an American musician and singer-songwriter and the lead vocalist of the punk rock band the Ramones.\n- Miles Hunt was born on July 29, 1966, in Birmingham.\n- Miles Hunt is an English singer, songwriter, and guitarist.\n- Vent 414 was chiefly noted for a lineup that included Miles Hunt of The Wonder Stuff, Billy Duffy of The Cult, Morgan Nicholls of Senseless Things, The Streets, and Muse, and Pete Howard of The Clash and Eat.\n- Don't Worry About Me was the first album Joey Ramone released as a solo artist after his earlier releases with the Ramones as their lead singer.\n- Joey Ramone died on April 15, 2001.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "4a0be354-c1cd-5b34-aa40-9a1f57c2b47c",
